==Russian==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|zlato|lang=ru}} (Old Church Slavonic {{term|злато|tr=zlato|lang=cu}}), from {{proto|Indo-European|ghəl|lang=ru}}. Cognate with Ukrainian {{term|золото|tr=zoloto|lang=uk}}, Belarusian {{term|золата|tr=zolata|lang=be}}, Bulgarian {{term|злато|tr=zlato|lang=bg}}, Serbian {{term|злато|tr=zlato|lang=sh|sc=Cyrl}}, Slovene {{term|zlato|lang=sl}}, Czech {{term|zlato|lang=cs}}, Slovak {{term|zlato|lang=sk}}, Polish {{term|złoto|lang=pl}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{proto|Germanic|gulþan|lang=}} (whence English {{term|gold|lang=en}}).

